 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**If you’re healthy and just going out briefly, an N95 isn’t generally needed—but avoid strenuous or prolonged outdoor activity today.** Singapore’s NEA forecast for **Saturday, 17 October 2026** is PSI **150–230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy)**. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nIf you’ll be outside for a long time, or the current **1-hour PM2.5** reading is high, consider a well-fitting **N95, KN95, FFP2 or KF94**. Older adults, pregnant people, children, and people with heart or lung conditions should minimize or avoid outdoor activity; if they must go out, a mask may help when PM2.5 is high. Check your area’s live PM2.5 reading in NEA’s myENV app before heading out. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/others/haze/))",
